    {
      "type": "shaped",
      "_comment": "The stone hammer's head is COBBLESTONE, which is what mining stone yields; mining stone no longer drops stone itself. Copper hammers wait for their ingot to exist as an item. 'f' is the head material, '/' the stick, and a space (not '-') is an empty cell, the only empty marker the loader accepts.",
      "pattern": [" f ", " /f", "/  "],
      "key": { "f": "cobblestone", "/": "stick" },
      "result": { "block": "stone_hammer", "count": 1 }
    },
    {
      "type": "shaped",
      "_comment": "The iron tools, built from the ingot the iron_ingot item provides. Shapes are the stone hammer's and the wooden pickaxe's: the hammer's head is the 'f' cell and the pickaxe is three ingots over two sticks.",
      "pattern": [" f ", " /f", "/  "],
      "key": { "f": "iron_ingot", "/": "stick" },
      "result": { "block": "iron_hammer", "count": 1 }
    },
    {
      "type": "shaped",
      "pattern": ["III", " S ", " S "],
      "key": { "I": "iron_ingot", "S": "stick" },
      "result": { "block": "iron_pickaxe", "count": 1 }
    },
    {
      "type": "shaped",
      "_comment": "The empty bucket, the third thing the iron ingot buys: three ingots in a V, the classic shape, because an empty bucket has no other way to exist and the fill/pour loop needs one.",
      "pattern": ["I I", " I "],
      "key": { "I": "iron_ingot" },
      "result": { "block": "bucket", "count": 1 }
    },
    {
      "type": "shaped",
      "_comment": "The wooden tools. A key entry may LIST several ingredients, any of which fills the cell: the loader expands the recipe into one concrete recipe per combination, so matching stays exact and a tool is always ONE wood type throughout (oak head on a pine handle matches nothing). 3 cells a side, so these are crafting-table recipes like the stone hammer above.",
      "pattern": ["PPP", " S ", " S "],
      "key": { "P": ["oak_planks", "pine_planks", "spruce_planks", "holly_planks"], "S": "stick" },
